 ## Overview
-Multi-scale Neural Field Reconstruction is a framework that constructs pyramid-structured encoding volumes to provide geometric information at all scales for Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF), addressing the limitation of single-scale volumes in scenes with diverse object sizes [S1, unofficial]. It learns an encoding volume and reconstructs density and radiance fields separately, using multi-scale geometric information acquired during training (rendering at each level) and used only at the final level during testing [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from siblings like [Explicit Radiance Fields](806-explicit-radiance-fields.md) by explicitly modeling scale via a pyramid of 3D volumes rather than a single grid or octree, and from [Plenoxels](7440-plenoxels.md) by retaining differentiable neural field reconstruction at each scale rather than relying on spherical harmonics or explicit voxel colors directly.
